/* @catalog — generated by `npm run catalog:generate`; do not edit by hand.
 * Internal
 *   Types: Sent
 *   Functions: mount, chosen, pick, readBytes, keyOf, serveUploads, staged, previews, uploadButton, ready,
 *              besideDialog
 *   Constants: item, operationId, png, gif, uploadId
 * Tests
 *   - ready source cover selection captures both revisions and requires separate approval; cleanup pending is confirmed success
 *   - after reopening, only the initiating administrator can reconcile original cover receipt without generating a new key
 *   - clear cover is separately confirmed and a lost response retains DELETE plus original payload
 *   - cancelling an unconfirmed operation requires explicit review and retries its new immutable cancellation UUID
 *   - cancelled cleanup can be reconciled by another administrator and absent owner is never fabricated
 *   - a confirmed cancellation cannot reopen an obsolete approval from a delayed operations read
 *   - editing disabled retains an explicit current-revision cancellation and its cleanup receipt
 *   - a capability change invalidates an already open new cover approval before any write
 *   - a source import saved by a newer release refuses the cover change with a reload request and no retry
 *   - the upload button sits beside Choose and is disabled offline, without editing, with an unresolved operation and while an upload runs
 *   - a file that is not a JPG, PNG or WebP by its bytes, or is empty, is refused locally and nothing is sent
 *   - an upload opens the existing confirmation with a proportional preview; Cancel sends nothing and a new choice is a new intent; confirm sends the upload
 *   - an item changed while the upload confirmation is open disables confirm
 *   - an upload retried after the item changed opens an enabled confirmation bound to the item as it is then
 *   - an unknown outcome keeps the intent: Retry resends the same key and bytes after the file becomes unreadable, an unconfirmed receipt keeps it, and Cancel forgets it
 *   - a successful upload answered after leaving Admin view opens no confirmation
 *   - a response this bundle cannot parse asks for a reload instead of a Retry and opens no confirmation
 *   - an upload confirmed while another cover approval is open leaves that approval in place, waits as Use this image and is dropped when that approval succeeds
 *   - an upload finishing while another page dialog is open stacks no second dialog and offers Use this image instead
 *   - Use this image opens the waiting upload's confirmation with its preview, whose Cancel returns focus to the upload button, and confirming it sends that upload
 *   - a view change or a new upload drops a waiting upload, and with no dialog open an upload opens its confirmation at once as before
 *   - leaving the page with an upload confirmation open revokes its preview
 * @end-catalog */

